# /filing/:id is the one private route with a DYNAMIC segment, so postbuild
# cannot write it a 200 shell the way it does for /dashboard and /intake: there
# is no file to write, the id is different every time. Cloudflare then answers
# it out of 404.html, which is how a filer returning from Dodo checkout, whose
# return URL is exactly this path, ended up watching a tab titled "Page not
# found" while verify-payment ran behind it. The page itself always rendered.
# Above the catch-all because rules are matched in order.
/filing/:id   /index.html   200

